---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  ["introduction", "Introduction"],
  ["information", "What we collect"],
  ["local", "What stays on your devices"],
  ["sharing", "Who else is involved"],
  ["choices", "Your choices"],
  ["children", "Children"],
  ["updates", "Updates to this policy"],
  ["contact", "Contact"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy | Ankiel Code"
  description="How Ankiel Code handles information: no telemetry, no analytics, and no account."
  heading="Ankiel Code Privacy Policy"
  lede="Ankiel Code is self-hosted software. It has no accounts and sends no telemetry, analytics, or crash reports. This policy covers the little that passes through code.ankiel.com."
  effectiveDate="2026-11-24"
  lastUpdated="2026-11-24"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="introduction">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      Ankiel Code is open-source software that you run yourself. This Privacy Policy (the “Policy”)
      describes the information handled when you use the Ankiel Code desktop, mobile, and web
      applications, the hosted web client at{" "}<a href="https://app.code.ankiel.com">https://app.code.ankiel.com</a>,
      or the website at{" "}<a href="https://code.ankiel.com">https://code.ankiel.com</a> (the “Site”). “We” means the
      maintainer of Ankiel Code.
    </p>
    <p>
      This Policy does not govern the coding agents, AI providers, or machines you connect to Ankiel
      Code. They process information under their own terms and privacy policies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="information">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>What We Collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No account.</strong> Ankiel Code does not ask you to sign up or sign in to anything we
        operate.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No telemetry.</strong> The apps and the server send no analytics, usage data, or crash
        reports to us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Request logs.</strong> When you load the Site, download a release, check for an update, or
        open the hosted web client, our hosting and content-delivery providers receive ordinary
        request data such as your IP address, user agent, requested URL, and timestamp. We use it to
        deliver and secure these services, not for advertising.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What you send us.</strong> If you open a GitHub issue, discussion, or pull request, or
        otherwise contact us, we see what you choose to include.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not use your source code, prompts, or agent responses to train AI models, and we do not
      have access to them: they travel between your clients, your machine, and the providers you
      configure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="local">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>What Stays on Your Devices</h2>
    <p>
      Ankiel Code stores connection settings, credentials, preferences, drafts, and cached thread,
      file, branch, and server metadata on your devices and on the machine that runs your server.
      Credentials and session tokens use platform-provided protected storage where supported. This
      information is not sent to us.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Camera.</strong> Used only when you scan a pairing QR code. Frames are processed on
        your device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Photos and files.</strong> Items you select are accessed only to preview them or
        attach them to a request you start.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local network.</strong> Used to discover or connect to servers reachable from your
        device.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Who Else Is Involved</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Providers you choose.</strong> At your direction, prompts, files, and related content
      are sent to the coding agents and AI providers configured on your machine.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Infrastructure.</strong> The Site, release downloads, and update feeds are served through
      third-party hosting and content-delivery providers, such as Cloudflare and Vercel, and source code and
      releases are hosted on GitHub. The mobile app is delivered through Apple and Google app stores
      and may fetch updates through Expo. Each processes information under its own privacy policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal information and we do not use it for targeted advertising. We do not
      respond to browser “Do Not Track” signals because we do not track you across sites.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="choices">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can disconnect servers and clear local caches from Settings, revoke camera, photo, and
      local-network permissions in your device settings, and delete everything by uninstalling the
      app. The mobile app has cache controls under <strong>Settings → App → Client Storage</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      To ask what we hold about you or to request deletion, open an issue or contact us through{" "}<a
        href="https://github.com/benank/ankielcode/issues">GitHub</a
      >. Because we collect so little, the answer is usually server logs held by our hosting providers
      and anything you sent us directly. We cannot delete information held by your own machines or by
      AI providers; contact them directly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <p class="section-number">06</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Ankiel Code is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information from them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="updates">
    <p class="section-number">07</p>
    <h2>Updates to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Policy. Changes take effect when the revised Policy is posted at this URL, and
      we will update the dates above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">08</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or requests about this Policy: open an issue at{" "}<a class="contact-link"
        href="https://github.com/benank/ankielcode/issues">github.com/benank/ankielcode/issues</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
